    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1565">

                <pb facs="0998" n="882" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg882"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/96.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The French Ambassador to Counselor Lansing.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">French Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 17, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Counselor</hi>: I have received from the
                    Boleo Company a telegram stating that serious troubles have apparently begun
                    once more at Santa Rosalia, the Mexican garrison having, it is reported,
                    revolted and the life of the employees of the company being threatened.</p>
                <p>If it were possible for the American Government to ascertain how the matter
                    stands and to supply such protection as may be needed, I should be very much
                    obliged. The same has been done before and my Government has highly appreciated
                    the usefulness of your intervention. I hope it will be possible to act again as
                    was previously done.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jusserand</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
